# Security Policy

**Please do not report security vulnerabilities publicly.**

If you believe you have found a security vulnerability in {{ project.title }}, please report it through GitHub's
[Private Vulnerability Reporting](https://github.com/sonata-project/{{ project.repository.name }}/security/advisories/new).

Do not use the public issue tracker to report security vulnerabilities. Reports submitted through Private
Vulnerability Reporting are confidential and only accessible to the repository maintainers.

Please provide as much information as possible to help us understand and reproduce the issue, including the affected
versions, the steps to reproduce and a proof of concept if available.

If you are not sure whether an issue has security implications, please report it privately.

The Sonata Project maintainers will assess the report and coordinate the investigation, the fix and the disclosure of
confirmed vulnerabilities. Please do not disclose the vulnerability publicly until a fix has been released and the
disclosure has been coordinated with the maintainers.
